.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECK-STATIC 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-check-static
.Nd check scoped source syntax, Rust lints and native boundary records
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-static.py
.Nm python3 scripts/check-static.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3 scripts/check-static.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This is a source-checkout developer command.
The manual title does not name an installed executable.
Run with POSIX Python 3.10 or newer and the separately provisioned
Rust 1.98.0 toolchain, rustfmt and clippy-driver.
Only the macOS arm64 tool identities in docs/static-tools.json are reviewed.
The command resolves the checkout from its own location.
It compiles selected Python source without executing it or writing bytecode,
compares the pinned Rust formatter output for two host test files, and runs
Clippy's default group on those harnesses and their pure imported modules.
It also checks the native boundary inventory for changed hashes or site lists.
.Pp
Python syntax is not semantic analysis.
The boundary scan is change detection, not a proof of soundness.
No native trap module is executed or formatted.
Metadata and copied inputs live in temporary directories removed on exit.
Each trusted tool call has a ten-second deadline and a 4 MiB merged-output
cap;
only the owned, non-detaching process group is terminated on failure.
Sources are limited to 1 MiB each, 1,000 files and 16 MiB total.
Tool and source identities are rechecked during the run.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without performing the check.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the command version and exit.
This is not a published sys-init release identifier.
.El
.Pp
There are no ordinary operands, repair modes or output-directory options.
.Sh OUTPUT
Success and caught operational failures produce JSON on standard output with
schema sys-init-static-v1 and a result of pass, fail or blocked.
A failure also writes an escaped diagnostic on standard error.
Success includes tool/source identities, file counts and Clippy diagnostics.
Ordinary Rust warnings can remain visible without a Clippy-group failure.
.Pp
Formatting differences require source review using the pinned formatter
options.
Restore the reviewed tool installation or separately review a tool-lock update
when identity checks fail; do not replace a digest merely to silence a
failure.
Source boundary drift requires renewed source review before updating its
record.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The inherited PATH and rustup configuration locate the installed toolchain.
The platform and machine determine which reviewed tool hashes apply.
Temporary-file placement follows the host Python tempfile configuration.
No tools are downloaded or installed.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa docs/static-tools.json
Tool identities, source scope and compiler/formatter arguments.
.It Pa docs/native-boundaries.json
Reviewed native source hashes and textual boundary occurrences.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All scoped checks passed; also help and version.
.It 1
Caught source, format, lint, output-limit or other operational failure.
.It 2
A required tool or reviewed host is unavailable or mismatched, or a tool times
out.
.It 64
Invalid arguments, with diagnostics on standard error.
.El
.Pp
Unexpected interpreter failures or abrupt termination can produce a nonzero
exit without a normal result.
An absent result is not success.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the sys-init repository root with prerequisites already provisioned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-static.py --help
python3 scripts/check-static.py
.Ed
.Pp
The first invocation prints usage and exits zero.
The second prints the success JSON and exits zero only if its scoped checks
pass.
To exercise argument rejection without changing inputs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-static.py --unknown
.Ed
.Pp
This prints diagnostics on standard error and exits 64.
No root privileges are required by these examples.
Use python3 scripts/check-all.py to retain the normal check and its logs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository references: docs/STATIC-CHECKS.md and
docs/NATIVE-BOUNDARY-REVIEW.md,
docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
Render this source with the host mandoc tool for offline terminal reading.
.Sh CAVEATS
Independent technical and reader review, installed-target lookup and release
approval remain separate.
This check does not establish runtime conformance.
.Sh RECORD VALIDATION
Settings and boundary records require exact schemas, fields and types before
any tool lookup.
Each JSON input is limited to 1 MiB and 32 nesting levels; duplicate keys,
non-finite values, invalid paths/digests and malformed fields reject.
Collections have at most 1,000 entries and strings at most 4,096 characters.
See docs/STATIC-RECORDS.md for complete rules and remaining filesystem limits.
Malformed records follow the existing failed JSON and exit-1 contract.
.Pp
Decision 0114 requires ordinary selected source and JSON files, rejects symlink
components within the supplied root, and checks identity around bounded reads.
Record bytes captured before tools must match a final reread before success.
This is not an atomic snapshot or a general filesystem-I/O deadline.
